      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "RAW AI DENOISE  (Lightroom-style)\n\n1. On 'Load RAW Image' click  \ud83d\udcc2 Choose RAW file(s)\u2026  and pick your ARW / CR3 / NEF / RAF ... files (Ctrl- or Shift-click for several). You can also drag files from Explorer/Finder onto that node. They are copied into ComfyUI/input/raw.\n\n2. Press Run. The first run downloads the AI model (58 MB) into models/raw_denoise.\n   Picked several files? Run processes the one shown in raw_file; '\u25b6 Queue all N selected files' processes every one of them.\n\n3. 'RAW AI Denoise' works on the raw sensor data (denoise + demosaic in one pass, like Lightroom). Amount works like Lightroom's slider (default 50). Changing only Amount / color_noise re-uses the cached network result, so tuning is quick.\n\n4. 'Save Linear DNG' writes <name>-Enhanced-NR.dng to ComfyUI/output/raw_denoise (clear output_folder to save next to the original). Open it in Lightroom / Camera Raw and edit it like a raw file.\n\n5. Check the 100% crop on the right (move center_x / center_y). The 16-bit TIFF saver is bypassed - select it and press Ctrl+B to enable it.\n\nIf something fails, the error message says why (most often: the 'rawpy' package isn't installed in ComfyUI's own Python - see README)."
      ],
      "title": "How to use",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
